{
  "raw": {
    "https://stcatherine.peopleadmin.com/postings/11127": {
      "title": "St. Catherine Employment Site | Simulated Participant Educator (SPE) &amp; Administrative Coordinator",
      "description": "St. Catherine Employment Site | Simulated Participant Educator (SPE) &amp; Administrative Coordinator Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help St. Catherine University Home Page Benefits Strategic Plan Simulated Participant Educator (SPE) & Administrative Coordinator Bookmark this Hiring Approval Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Title Simulated Participant Educator (SPE) & Administrative Coordinator Division Academic Affairs Department/Office Interprofessional Education Position Summary Information Advertisement The Interprofessional Education Program at St. Catherine University invites applications for a full-time Simulated Participant Educator ( SPE ) & Administrative Coordinator position. This position provides administrative coordination for the Institute of Simulation and Interprofessional Learning (I- SAIL ) and serves as the team’s primary Simulated Participant (SP) Educator. The position coordinates all aspects of the human simulation program; plans and leads SP coaching sessions in collaboration with faculty and other key partners; serves as the primary point of contact for SPs; and provides SP prebriefing, event-day management, debriefing, and ongoing support. The position also supports healthcare simulation accreditation, simulation and interprofessional education ( IPE ) operations, departmental communications, program evaluation and quality improvement, annual collaboration events, the Annual IPE conference, and other I- SAIL initiatives. Duties will include: Administrative Coordination for Simulation and IPE Manage simulation registration, IPE event registration, and sign-up processes Document and track simulation activities and IPE co-curricular activities Manage delegated departmental email accounts and route requests appropriately Complete PCard and out-of-pocket purchases and expense reconciliations for I- SAIL purchases. Coordinate departmental packages and mail Collect data and maintain organized electronic files and archives of departmental documentation Compile and upload materials supporting healthcare simulation accreditation Coordinate event logistics, including room scheduling, flyers, catering, sign-in processes, and continuing education certificate distribution Manage I- SAIL priority-designation spaces within the University’s event management system Build and distribute simulation and IPE surveys used to assess program outcomes Assist with evaluation data-management and quality improvement activities Assist with writing, formatting, proofreading, and distributing reports and outcomes, including annual reports, program-evaluation reports, and external marketing materials Collaborate with faculty lab manager to coordinate ordering of consumables across HSSHS and SoN programs Assist the IPE Director with IPE co-curricular scheduling Support updates to and management of the I- SAIL intranet site Produce and store meeting minutes for all meetings within the department (full department, committee level, advisory councils, etc.) Serve as I-SAIL’s primary SP Educator and principal point of contact for SPs throughout recruitment, onboarding, preparation, participation, and follow-up. Coordinate the full human simulation workflow, including SP outreach, recruitment, selection, matching, scheduling, confirmations, case-material distribution, and event follow-up. Plan, organize, and lead SP coaching sessions, co-facilitating with faculty, simulation specialists, or other key partners as appropriate. Collaborate with faculty and I- SAIL team members to clarify learning objectives, SP portrayal expectations, feedback responsibilities, boundaries, event flow, and performance expectations before coaching and events. Prepare and send clear, timely SP communications, including role offers, coaching and event details, case materials, maps, parking instructions, attire guidance, schedules, and required forms. Coordinate SP-related logistics, including rooms, meals and refreshments, parking, access, signage, consultant documentation and payments, supplies, and day-of arrival needs. Provide or coordinate SP orientation and prebriefing, including expectations, psychological and physical safety, confidentiality, boundaries, stop/pause processes, event flow, and feedback guidance. Manage SPs during simulation events by welcoming and checking them in, confirming readiness, maintaining schedules and room assignments, troubleshooting concerns, and coordinating with faculty and other I- SAIL team members. Support SPs with moulage, supplies, costuming, robing and disrobing, accessibility needs, and other role-specific preparations. Facilitate SP debriefing, de-roling, checkout, and follow-up after events, with support from other I- SAIL team members as needed. Coach SPs in providing learner-centered verbal or written feedback when feedback is part of the learning activity. Maintain accurate SP records, availability, participation history, training completion, payments, and other program documentation using approved systems. Gather feedback from SPs, faculty, learners, and team members and contribute to continuous improvement, quality assurance, and consistent SP methodology across I- SAIL . Promote an inclusive, respectful, accountable environment for SPs and promptly elevate concerns related to safety, boundaries, performance, or program quality. Order office supplies and materials supporting simulation and IPE programs. Order books, course materials, keys, and computers for faculty and adjuncts. Submit ServiceNow requests on behalf of the department. Provide copying and printing support for the I- SAIL team. Welcome and support students participating in I- SAIL events. Support technology, including Zoom rooms, for IPE co-curricular events. Pick up and distribute departmental packages and mail. Answer and route telephone calls and student inquiries. Minimum Qualifications Experience communicating effectively with diverse stakeholders through multiple methods, including email, telephone, virtual platforms, and in-person interaction. Experience facilitating training, orientation, coaching, or group learning activities. Experience handling sensitive and confidential information appropriately. Experience organizing, prioritizing, and completing multiple responsibilities within established guidelines and deadlines. Proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite and Google Workspace. Ability to learn and navigate information systems, databases, scheduling tools, and communication platforms. Ability to provide clear, constructive feedback and support participants before, during, and after learning activities. Ability to work collaboratively while independently managing assigned programs, communications, and event logistics. Preferred Qualifications Associate degree, bachelor’s degree, or some college coursework. Experience in simulated participant methodology, healthcare simulation, standardized patient education, adult learning, training, or facilitation. Experience working in higher education, healthcare, or a community-engaged educational program. Experience supporting prebriefing, feedback, debriefing, or participant well-being following emotionally or physically demanding learning activities. Familiarity with simulation standards of best practice, SP program operations, or healthcare simulation accreditation. EEO Statement Compensation: Hourly wage is $20.42 – $28.59 depending on qualifications and experience. The salary range listed reflects a good-faith estimate of what we reasonably anticipate to pay for this position, based on market data and internal equity, at the time of posting. Actual compensation will be determined based on qualifications, experience, skills, and other relevant factors. St. Catherine reserves the right to modify or adjust compensation depending on University needs. Benefits: Employees at St. Kate’s feel a deep connection to the University’s Mission and Vision, and they live their values at work. Benefits available to full-time employees include: Fourteen (14) paid holidays and paid “gift” days when the University is closed. Free tuition for employees and reduced tuition for their families after one year of service Health, dental, and vision insurance 403b retirement plan access Accrued sick time Specific information on all of our available benefits for full-time employees can be found HERE . St. Catherine University is an equal opportunity employer. Our commitment to inclusion reflects the central value of the Sisters of St. Joseph of Carondelet to “love of neighbor without distinction” and provides a learning and working environment that is enriched by the diversity of all our members. Individuals of all religious, racial, ethnic, gender identity, nation of origin, or disability groups are encouraged to apply. Should you need an interview accommodation please contact us at hr@stkate.edu or 651-690-6565. Application instructions for STAFF Visit St. Kate Careers to apply. Three references and successful completion of a background check will be required for employment. St. Catherine University 2004 Randolph Avenue, St. Paul, MN 55105 Equal Opportunity Employer / Drug Free Workplace / Tobacco Free Workplace Our university is a proud member of the Upper Midwest HERC and is committed to recruiting and retaining outstanding faculty and staff and assisting dual career couples. For more information and to find other higher education jobs in the Upper Midwest region, visit: www.uppermidwestherc.org. Posting Detail Information Posting Number 20220853-STAFF Posting Start Date 09/01/2026 Application Deadline 09/15/2026 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is your highest level of completed education? Some high school High school diploma or GED Some college Associate's degree Bachelor's degree Some graduate school Master's degree ABD Professional degree (e.g., JD, MD) Doctoral degree * Are you presently legally authorized to work in the United States for any U.S. employer? Please be aware that St. Catherine University is only able to consider candidates who are authorized to work in the United States. Yes No * St. Catherine University welcomes applications from candidates who are traditionally under-represented. We are happy to consider candidates who are currently in possession of a temporary work visa, however, please be aware that we do not offer employment visa sponsorship. Will you now or in the future require an employer to sponsor you for an employment-based visa/status in the U.S. (e.g. H-1B status)? Yes No Maybe * Can you perform the essential functions of this position with or without accommodation? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Professional Reference Contact Information Optional Documents Cover Letter Other Document 1 Other Document 2 2004 Randolph Avenue St. Paul, MN 55105 800-945-4599 651-690-6000 Human Resources Derham Hall 113 651-690-6565 hr@stkate.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://stcatherine.peopleadmin.com/postings/11092": {
      "title": "St. Catherine Employment Site",
      "description": "St. Catherine Employment Site | Public Safety Supervisor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help St. Catherine University Home Page Benefits Strategic Plan Public Safety Supervisor Bookmark this Hiring Approval Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Title Public Safety Supervisor Division Finance & Administration Department/Office Security Position Summary Information Advertisement St. Catherine University invites applications for a Public Safety Supervisor within the Public Safety Department. The Public Safety Department is committed to fostering a safe and welcoming environment for students, staff, faculty, and visitors. Our team takes a proactive, prevention-focused approach to campus safety, with officers on duty 24/7 to provide assistance and ensure the security of our campus community. The Public Safety Supervisor shall insure that all policies and procedures are followed, proper notifications are made, and proper documentation is prepared. The Public Safety Supervisor may also be responsible for scheduling staff, ensuring safety details are assigned and completed as assigned, maintaining uniforms, equipment, found and confiscated property, security office organization, reference material, and office files and fulfilling other duties as assigned. The Public Safety Supervisor also has “On-Call” duty, which is on a rotating schedule with their fellow supervisors. Responsibilities: Assigns duties and responsibilities to Public Safety Officers including scheduling shifts and training on day to day responsibilities Performs routine patrol functions and assists on-duty officers Evaluates performance for assigned Public Safety Officers Provides staff commendations Performs coaching, counseling and corrective measures as needed Ensures campus electronic access is functioning properly and diagnoses any problems Take inventory and issue equipment to officers Run, review, scrub and submit accurate reports Complete incident reports and review incident reports on a daily basis Ensure that reports are investigated in a timely manner and that all leads are followed Ensure that cameras are working and footage is saved and added to reports Develop and/or implement crime prevention programs and education. (i.e. Self-defense, alcohol awareness, fire safety, etc.) Plan, coordinate, & staff of special events or requests. (i.e. Orientation, Commencement, Move-In Day) Employees at St. Kate’s feel a deep connection to the University’s Mission and Vision, and they live their values at work. Benefits available to full-time employees include: Fourteen (14) paid holidays and paid “gift” days when the University is closed. Free tuition for employees and reduced tuition for their families after one year of service Health, dental, and vision insurance 403b retirement plan access Accrued sick time Paid parental leave after one year of service Specific information on all of our available benefits for full-time employees can be found HERE . St. Catherine University in St. Paul/Minneapolis, Minnesota, is a comprehensive Catholic university and home to one of the nation’s largest colleges for women, with associate and graduate programs for all genders. Founded by the Sisters of St. Joseph of Carondelet in 1905, the University integrates liberal arts and professional education within the Catholic traditions of intellectual inquiry and social teaching. Committed to excellence and opportunity, St. Catherine enrolls students in certificate, associate, baccalaureate, master’s and doctoral programs in traditional day and evening/weekend/online formats. Minimum Qualifications A current and valid driver’s license with an eligible driving record Computer skills in the Google and Microsoft Office suite AND EITHER : High School diploma Four years of Public Safety Officer experience or Resident Assistant (RA) experience can substitute for up to one year of PSO experience OR: Associate’s degree Two years of Public Safety Officer experience or Resident Assistant (RA) experience can substitute for up to six months of PSO experience Preferred Qualifications We seek creative, adaptable staff who enjoy working in a university climate that promotes multicultural understanding and cultural fluency, consistent with the University’s mission and values. EEO Statement Compensation: Salary: $47,132 – $49,000 depending on qualifications and experience. The salary range listed reflects a good-faith estimate of what we reasonably anticipate to pay for this position, based on market data and internal equity, at the time of posting. Actual compensation will be determined based on qualifications, experience, skills, and other relevant factors. St. Catherine reserves the right to modify or adjust compensation depending on University needs. St. Catherine University is an equal opportunity employer. Our commitment to inclusion reflects the central value of the Sisters of St. Joseph of Carondelet to “love of neighbor without distinction” and provides a learning and working environment that is enriched by the diversity of all our members. Individuals of all religious, racial, ethnic, gender identity, nation of origin, or disability groups are encouraged to apply. Should you need an interview accommodation please contact us at hr@stkate.edu or 651-690-6565. Application instructions for STAFF Visit St. Kate Careers to apply. Three references and successful completion of a background check will be required for employment. St. Catherine University 2004 Randolph Avenue, St. Paul, MN 55105 Equal Opportunity Employer / Drug Free Workplace / Tobacco Free Workplace Our university is a proud member of the Upper Midwest HERC and is committed to recruiting and retaining outstanding faculty and staff and assisting dual career couples. For more information and to find other higher education jobs in the Upper Midwest region, visit: www.uppermidwestherc.org. Posting Detail Information Posting Number 20220742-STAFF Posting Start Date 08/26/2026 Application Deadline 09/09/2026 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is your highest level of completed education? Some high school High school diploma or GED Some college Associate's degree Bachelor's degree Some graduate school Master's degree ABD Professional degree (e.g., JD, MD) Doctoral degree * St. Kate’s is committed to making Inclusive Excellence a reality and has identified “Drive a Culture of Inclusive Excellence” as one of six priorities in the strategic plan. Give a brief, specific example of how you have promoted a culture that values diversity, equity and inclusion in your current or recent role(s). (Open Ended Question) * For any education beyond high school, please list the degree or certification and the area of focus. (Open Ended Question) * Are you presently legally authorized to work in the United States for any U.S. employer? Please be aware that St. Catherine University is only able to consider candidates who are authorized to work in the United States. Yes No * St. Catherine University welcomes applications from candidates who are traditionally under-represented. We are happy to consider candidates who are currently in possession of a temporary work visa, however, please be aware that we do not offer employment visa sponsorship. Will you now or in the future require an employer to sponsor you for an employment-based visa/status in the U.S. (e.g. H-1B status)? Yes No Maybe * Can you perform the essential functions of this position with or without accommodation? Yes No * How did you hear about this opportunity? St. Catherine University website St. Catherine University employee Academic Jobs American College Personnel Association (ACPA) Association of Catholic Colleges/Universities Association of Student Affairs at Catholic Colleges and Universities Chronicle of Higher Education College or University website Council of Independent Colleges DisabilityConnect.com Diverse:  Issues in Higher Education DiversityConnect.com Facebook Google Jobs HigherEdJobs Higher Education Case Managers Association (HECMA) Higher Education Recruitment Consortium (HERC) Hispanic Outlook on Education Magazine IMDiversity Indeed Inside Higher Ed Insight Into Diversity Latinos in Higher Ed LGBTConnect.com LGBTQ in Higher Education LinkedIn Minnesota College Professionals Association Minnesota Council of Nonprofits MinnesotaWorks.net/Minnesota Workforce Center Minority Jobs NAFSA:  Association of International Educators National Association of Independent Colleges and Universities National Association of Student Personnel Administrators (NASPA) National Conference on Race and Ethnicity (NCORE) OutandEqual.com People of Color in Higher Education Pioneer Press Pollen Midwest Saint Paul Chamber of Commerce (SPACC) SimplyHired.com Star Tribune StudentAffairs.com Twin Cities Senior Student Affairs Officers listserv Twitter VeteransConnect.com Women in Higher Education ZipRecruiter Other Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents 2004 Randolph Avenue St. Paul, MN 55105 800-945-4599 651-690-6000 Human Resources Derham Hall 113 651-690-6565 hr@stkate.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
