    "https://stcatherine.peopleadmin.com/postings/11103": {
      "title": "St. Catherine Employment Site | Katie Central Coordinator",
      "description": "St. Catherine Employment Site | Katie Central Coordinator Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help St. Catherine University Home Page Benefits Strategic Plan Katie Central Coordinator Bookmark this Hiring Approval Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Title Katie Central Coordinator Division Academic Affairs Department/Office Academic Success Center Position Summary Information Advertisement The Office of Academic Success at St. Catherine University invites applications for a full-time Katie Central Coordinator position. The Katie Central Coordinator provides integrated student services to the main areas of records, enrollment, billing and financial aid. This role delivers high-quality customer service while guiding students through institutional processes related to enrollment, finances, and academic progress. Katie Central Coordinators take ownership of student inquiries from initial contact through resolution, ensuring consistent follow-through and coordination across offices. Through an advisor-informed approach, Coordinators help students understand their options, navigate challenges, and make informed decisions—particularly as they relate to persistence, affordability, and academic success. Responsibilities include: Serve as a primary point of contact for students and families via in-person, phone, email, and virtual communication. Provide timely, accurate, and student-centered responses to questions related to registration, billing, financial aid, and academic processes. Guide students through institutional systems and processes with clarity, patience, and attention to individual needs. Utilize an “advisor-lite” approach to help students understand options, implications, and next steps, particularly in relation to enrollment and financial decisions. Deliver high-quality customer service, especially in complex, sensitive, or high-stress situations, demonstrating empathy and professionalism. Take ownership of student inquiries and concerns from initial contact through resolution, ensuring follow-through and closure. Coordinate with partner offices (Financial Aid, Registrar, Student Accounts, Academic Advising) to resolve student issues while maintaining engagement with the student. Conduct warm handoffs when escalation is required, ensuring continuity of support and clear communication. Support students navigating multi-step or complex processes, including financial aid requirements, registration barriers, and account concerns. Help students think through affordability, timelines, and available options, connecting them to appropriate resources as needed. Assist students with key processes, including: Registration support (add/drop, approved late adds, overrides) Financial aid documentation and next steps Billing navigation, payment plans, and account review Transcript and enrollment verification requests Explain institutional policies and procedures clearly while operating within defined boundaries (no independent policy decisions or financial transactions). Maintain and update student records within institutional systems as appropriate. Provide general guidance on financial aid concepts (e.g., cost of attendance, SAP , Pell eligibility) and refer students for specialized support when needed. Conduct proactive outreach to students regarding key deadlines, missing requirements, and enrollment milestones. Document all student interactions, actions taken, and outcomes using established tracking tools. Identify and share trends, recurring student challenges, and process barriers with leadership to support continuous improvement. Reinforce messaging from partner offices to ensure consistent, clear communication to students. Minimum Qualifications Experience working in higher education of customer service fields Excellent written and oral communication skills Sensitive to cultural diversity and ability to community and interact with people from all backgrounds Experience navigating ambiguity and working within complex systems High level of customer services experience Preferred Qualifications Knowledge of a one-stop or related enrollment processes including but no limited to financial aid, student accounts, registrar functions and academic advising. Proven ability to work effectively with a team. Ability to analyze data and information and make informed, independent decisions. Highly motivated and results oriented. EEO Statement Compensation: Annual wage is $42,474 – $59,467 depending on qualifications and experience. The salary range listed reflects a good-faith estimate of what we reasonably anticipate to pay for this position, based on market data and internal equity, at the time of posting. Actual compensation will be determined based on qualifications, experience, skills, and other relevant factors. St. Catherine reserves the right to modify or adjust compensation depending on University needs. Benefits: Employees at St. Kate’s feel a deep connection to the University’s Mission and Vision, and they live their values at work. Benefits available to full-time employees include: Fourteen (14) paid holidays and paid “gift” days when the University is closed. Free tuition for employees and reduced tuition for their families after one year of service Health, dental, and vision insurance 403b retirement plan access Accrued sick time Specific information on all of our available benefits for full-time employees can be found HERE . St. Catherine University is an equal opportunity employer. Our commitment to inclusion reflects the central value of the Sisters of St. Joseph of Carondelet to “love of neighbor without distinction” and provides a learning and working environment that is enriched by the diversity of all our members. Individuals of all religious, racial, ethnic, gender identity, nation of origin, or disability groups are encouraged to apply. Should you need an interview accommodation please contact us at hr@stkate.edu or 651-690-6565. Application instructions for STAFF Visit St. Kate Careers to apply. Three references and successful completion of a background check will be required for employment. St. Catherine University 2004 Randolph Avenue, St. Paul, MN 55105 Equal Opportunity Employer / Drug Free Workplace / Tobacco Free Workplace Our university is a proud member of the Upper Midwest HERC and is committed to recruiting and retaining outstanding faculty and staff and assisting dual career couples. For more information and to find other higher education jobs in the Upper Midwest region, visit: www.uppermidwestherc.org. Posting Detail Information Posting Number 20220834-STAFF Posting Start Date 09/01/2026 Application Deadline 09/21/2026 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is your highest level of completed education? Some high school High school diploma or GED Some college Associate's degree Bachelor's degree Some graduate school Master's degree ABD Professional degree (e.g., JD, MD) Doctoral degree * Are you presently legally authorized to work in the United States for any U.S. employer? Please be aware that St. Catherine University is only able to consider candidates who are authorized to work in the United States. Yes No * St. Catherine University welcomes applications from candidates who are traditionally under-represented. We are happy to consider candidates who are currently in possession of a temporary work visa, however, please be aware that we do not offer employment visa sponsorship. Will you now or in the future require an employer to sponsor you for an employment-based visa/status in the U.S. (e.g. H-1B status)? Yes No Maybe * Can you perform the essential functions of this position with or without accommodation? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents 2004 Randolph Avenue St. Paul, MN 55105 800-945-4599 651-690-6000 Human Resources Derham Hall 113 651-690-6565 hr@stkate.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
