    "https://stcatherine.peopleadmin.com/postings/11107": {
      "title": "St. Catherine Employment Site",
      "description": "St. Catherine Employment Site | Facilities Maintenance Manager Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help St. Catherine University Home Page Benefits Strategic Plan Facilities Maintenance Manager Bookmark this Hiring Approval Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Title Facilities Maintenance Manager Division Finance & Administration Department/Office Steam Plant Position Summary Information Advertisement The Facilities Department at St. Catherine University invites applications for a full-time Facilities Maintenance Manager position. The Facilities Maintenance Manager is responsible for stewardship of the university’s physical properties across 1.1m square feet of building space. This includes academic, athletic, performing arts, residential, administrative facilities and a steam plant. The purpose of this position is to manage the operation, maintenance, repair, and long-term stewardship of the building systems and infrastructure that support the university’s missions. This role oversees maintenance planning, service delivery, and system reliability of mechanical, electrical, plumbing, and building-operating systems within campus buildings Ensure maintenance services are delivered safely and effectively, in alignment with university standards, customer expectations, regulatory requirements, and industry best practices. Lead maintenance planning for HVAC , electrical, plumbing and roof capital renewal projects to ensure maintainability, reliability, and lifecycle performance. Facilitate coordination among internal stakeholders, external engineering consultants, contractors, vendors, and regulatory agencies. Oversees invoicing with steam plant vendors and authorize purchases for plant supplies and equipment Provide supervision and developement for carpenters and painters, building a high-performing team. Minimum Qualifications Minimum of 5 years of experience in facilities maintenance operations including mechanical, electrical, and plumbing systems. Minimum of 3 years of experience in a maintenance supervision or managerial role Demonstrated ability to manage/coordinate multiple projects simultaneously. Knowledge of budgeting and financial management in a maintenance context. Excellent problem-solving and decision-making skills. Strong communication and interpersonal skills. Ability to work flexible hours, including weekends and holidays, as needed. Preferred Qualifications Proficiency with computerized maintenance management systems ( CMMS ), Microsoft Office and Google Suites. Proficiency with building automation system controls Experience with large HVAC replacement and retrocommissioning projects Experience in hiring and firing & contract negotiation EEO Statement Compensation: Annual wage is $65,000 – $85,000 depending on qualifications and experience. The salary range listed reflects a good-faith estimate of what we reasonably anticipate to pay for this position, based on market data and internal equity, at the time of posting. Actual compensation will be determined based on qualifications, experience, skills, and other relevant factors. St. Catherine reserves the right to modify or adjust compensation depending on University needs. Benefits: Employees at St. Kate’s feel a deep connection to the University’s Mission and Vision, and they live their values at work. Benefits available to full-time employees include: Fourteen (14) paid holidays and paid “gift” days when the University is closed. Free tuition for employees and reduced tuition for their families after one year of service Health, dental, and vision insurance 403b retirement plan access Accrued sick time Specific information on all of our available benefits for full-time employees can be found HERE . St. Catherine University is an equal opportunity employer. Our commitment to inclusion reflects the central value of the Sisters of St. Joseph of Carondelet to “love of neighbor without distinction” and provides a learning and working environment that is enriched by the diversity of all our members. Individuals of all religious, racial, ethnic, gender identity, nation of origin, or disability groups are encouraged to apply. Should you need an interview accommodation please contact us at hr@stkate.edu or 651-690-6565. Application instructions for STAFF Visit St. Kate Careers to apply. Three references and successful completion of a background check will be required for employment. St. Catherine University 2004 Randolph Avenue, St. Paul, MN 55105 Equal Opportunity Employer / Drug Free Workplace / Tobacco Free Workplace Our university is a proud member of the Upper Midwest HERC and is committed to recruiting and retaining outstanding faculty and staff and assisting dual career couples. For more information and to find other higher education jobs in the Upper Midwest region, visit: www.uppermidwestherc.org. Posting Detail Information Posting Number 20220856-STAFF Posting Start Date 08/28/2026 Application Deadline 10/14/2026 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is your highest level of completed education? Some high school High school diploma or GED Some college Associate's degree Bachelor's degree Some graduate school Master's degree ABD Professional degree (e.g., JD, MD) Doctoral degree * Are you presently legally authorized to work in the United States for any U.S. employer? Please be aware that St. Catherine University is only able to consider candidates who are authorized to work in the United States. Yes No * St. Catherine University welcomes applications from candidates who are traditionally under-represented. We are happy to consider candidates who are currently in possession of a temporary work visa, however, please be aware that we do not offer employment visa sponsorship. Will you now or in the future require an employer to sponsor you for an employment-based visa/status in the U.S. (e.g. H-1B status)? Yes No Maybe * Can you perform the essential functions of this position with or without accommodation? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Professional Reference Contact Information Optional Documents 2004 Randolph Avenue St. Paul, MN 55105 800-945-4599 651-690-6000 Human Resources Derham Hall 113 651-690-6565 hr@stkate.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://stcatherine.peopleadmin.com/postings/11022": {
      "title": "St. Catherine Employment Site",
      "description": "St. Catherine Employment Site | Front of House Staff Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help St. Catherine University Home Page Benefits Strategic Plan Front of House Staff Bookmark this Hiring Approval Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Title Front of House Staff Division Institutional Advancement Department/Office O'Shaughnessy Theater Position Summary Information Advertisement The The O’Shaughnessy Theater at St. Catherine University invites applications for part-time and on-call Front of House staff . The O’Shaughnessy’s usher core staff is made up of St. Kate’s students and on-call staff. This position supports event operations by performing a variety of front-of-house duties. Select team members, per supervisor’s discretion, are trained to perform multiple front-of-house roles, including Ticket Office Assistant and Usher. Role assignments vary based on event schedules, attendance, and operational needs, and employees may rotate between responsibilities during a shift or across different events. Most new hires begin as Ushers. As training is completed and operational needs require, employees may be assigned to additional front-of-house roles, including Ticket Office Assistant. This position is customer-facing and successful employees typically have an extroverted personality, strong verbal communication skills, and comfort interacting with members of the public. Minimum Qualifications ● Outgoing and enjoys interaction with the public ● Excellent communication skills, including written, verbal and interpersonal ● Strong customer service skills ● Punctual and reliable ● Ability to multitask ● Ability to think quickly and make decisions promptly ● Ability to react calmly and quickly in stressful situations ● Comfortable with technology ● Able to work weekends and evenings ● Understanding of basic bookkeeping skills, including working with sales (handling cash, making change, giving/keeping receipts), creating deposits, and balancing sales activity per event ● Work with others in a team setting ● Ability to listen and follow directions ● Must be able to climb stairs ● Must be able to stand ● Must be able to lift and carry boxes/items up to 30 lbs ● Able to work independently and be self-starter Preferred Qualifications ● Experience working in a performing arts venue ● Previous Audience View sales experience a plus, but not required; we will train EEO Statement Compensation: Hourly wage is $16.47. The salary range listed reflects a good-faith estimate of what we reasonably anticipate to pay for this position, based on market data and internal equity, at the time of posting. Actual compensation will be determined based on qualifications, experience, skills, and other relevant factors. St. Catherine reserves the right to modify or adjust compensation depending on University needs. St. Catherine University is an equal opportunity employer. Our commitment to inclusion reflects the central value of the Sisters of St. Joseph of Carondelet to “love of neighbor without distinction” and provides a learning and working environment that is enriched by the diversity of all our members. Individuals of all religious, racial, ethnic, gender identity, nation of origin, or disability groups are encouraged to apply. Should you need an interview accommodation please contact us at hr@stkate.edu or 651-690-6565. Application instructions for STAFF Visit St. Kate Careers to apply. Three references and successful completion of a background check will be required for employment. St. Catherine University 2004 Randolph Avenue, St. Paul, MN 55105 Equal Opportunity Employer / Drug Free Workplace / Tobacco Free Workplace Our university is a proud member of the Upper Midwest HERC and is committed to recruiting and retaining outstanding faculty and staff and assisting dual career couples. For more information and to find other higher education jobs in the Upper Midwest region, visit: www.uppermidwestherc.org. Posting Detail Information Posting Number 20220848-STAFF Posting Start Date 07/28/2026 Application Deadline 09/30/2026 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is your highest level of completed education? Some high school High school diploma or GED Some college Associate's degree Bachelor's degree Some graduate school Master's degree ABD Professional degree (e.g., JD, MD) Doctoral degree * Are you presently legally authorized to work in the United States for any U.S. employer? Please be aware that St. Catherine University is only able to consider candidates who are authorized to work in the United States. Yes No * St. Catherine University welcomes applications from candidates who are traditionally under-represented. We are happy to consider candidates who are currently in possession of a temporary work visa, however, please be aware that we do not offer employment visa sponsorship. Will you now or in the future require an employer to sponsor you for an employment-based visa/status in the U.S. (e.g. H-1B status)? Yes No Maybe * Can you perform the essential functions of this position with or without accommodation? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents 2004 Randolph Avenue St. Paul, MN 55105 800-945-4599 651-690-6000 Human Resources Derham Hall 113 651-690-6565 hr@stkate.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
